  "expectations": [
    {
      "text": "diagnosis attributes cmderr=3 to a Program-Buffer batch faulting - naming the CSR sweep hitting a caps over-claimed CSR (and/or mstatus.FS/VS Off for FPR/V sweeps) as the concrete cause on a new engine",
      "passed": true,
      "evidence": "cmderr=3 attributed to 'an instruction inside a Program-Buffer (PB) execution trapped'; concrete cause 1: 'The engine WARL-pins mstatus.FS/VS to Off, and the first fld/fsd / vsetvl/vle8.v/vse8.v in a PB raises illegal instruction -> cmderr=3'. The caps-over-claim/CSR-sweep pathway is kept as a cause to check (Cause 3: binary predating the bisect or non-reproducing batch; triage step 1 handles the renamed 'csr_sweep: CSR 0x...' branch). The raw-vs-renamed inference is code-grounded per the judgment note."
    },
    {
      "text": "playbook uses the csr_sweep bisect diagnostic (the error names the offending CSR) and fixes the gate in andes_caps.hpp to match the spec's IM Requirement, test-first",
      "passed": true,
      "evidence": "Triage step 1: 'If the message starts csr_sweep: CSR 0x... it is a caps over-claim'; Cause 3 fix: 'Rebuild from current source so the bisect names the CSR', then 'RED: ... assert the failing supports_csr() verdict' followed by 'GREEN: fix the case in andes_gate_for (src/hybrid/andes_caps.hpp) ... Gate on the SPEC's existence condition exactly, not a correlated feature'."
    },
    {
      "text": "playbook validates with a cold-cache rerun (clear ~/.cache/andesim so the baseline capture re-runs the sweep) and notes the --verify field count may legitimately drop",
      "passed": true,
      "evidence": "'rm -rf ~/.cache/andesim' cold-cache rerun in Cause-1 fix step 3 and Cause-3 step 3 ('cold-cache rerun; repeat until the capture is clean'); 'Expect the --verify field count to DROP by one per de-claimed CSR (correct: those were zero-vs-zero false matches)'. The doc also explains the cold-cache baseline capture 'runs a FULL drain with all sweeps on'."
    },
    {
      "text": "playbook does NOT recommend disabling the CSR sweep or tolerating the fault as the permanent fix",
      "passed": true,
      "evidence": "All three fixes are root-cause (rebuild the qemu.cfg pairing, fix the memory map, fix the caps gate); 'There is no correct workaround that skips the scratch page'; the only workaround is flagged 'Interim workaround only (no rebuild possible) ... Do not keep this'. Nowhere is disabling the sweep or tolerating the fault suggested."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "passed": 4,
    "failed": 0,
    "total": 4,
    "pass_rate": 1.0
  }
}

